WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.070
If you want to play a costumed superhero,
then you need to look the part, and that means

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.600
intense workouts coupled with an insane diet.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.160
Let's take a look at how Zachary Levi went
from supergeek to superhero, and got ripped

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.720
"Shazam!"

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.540
When Zachary Levi agreed to take on Shazam
as his next big role, he essentially agreed

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.180
to make the gym his second home.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.960
After all, this is a character who has stood
his ground in a number of scraps with Superman

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.720
over the years.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.640
If this confrontation is ever going to play
out on the big screen, then Levi has to at

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.700
least keep pace with Henry Cavill, assuming
Cavill is still playing the Man of Steel by

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.300
the time a crossover is viable.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:42.640
The movie's official synopsis even described
Shazam as having a "ripped, godlike body,"

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.000
so there's little wonder Levi began hitting
the weights almost every day.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.920
During a chat with former Smallville Lex Luthor
actor Michael Rosenbaum, Levi said he's working

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.520
out five or six days a week.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.520
He elaborated:

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.820
"Sometimes we'll do two-a-days and then more
off days.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.420
But typically, we'll just go, you know, hour-and-fifteen-minute
session every day."

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:06.250
That's a lot of gym time no matter who you
are, and all that time pumping iron definitely

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:06.740
shows.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.940
When someone who doesn't work out regularly
starts hitting the gym hard, they usually

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.260
experience what's known as "newbie gains."

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.120
"Yes, you too can have a body like mine, if
you're not careful."

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.420
This was evidently the case for Levi, who
managed to pack on an impressive amount of

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.340
pounds within his first six weeks of training.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.840
He told Rosenbaum in February 2018:

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.880
"Before I got the role, I was about 200 pounds.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.900
I've hovered around 200 pounds most of my
adult life."

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.580
Levi gave a similar account of his early gains
when Variety caught up with him almost a year

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:37.260
down the line.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:41.920
Speaking to the Hollywood trade at the New
York City premiere of The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.520
season 2, the actor revealed that he'd started
seeing results right away:

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.160
"I immediately put on about 24 pounds and
then we carved that down in about half.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:55.240
So I've been hovering around 215 pounds, and
I'm in the best shape of my life and stronger

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.320
and happier and healthier than I've ever been."

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:58.320
"What's going on?"

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.540
"Oh, well, I got into really good shape.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.240
Am I hitting the light right?"

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.400
"What is… what's happening?"

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.120
"Why?"

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:05.780
"Why?"

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:10.740
It probably won't surprise you to learn that
Levi had to consume a heroic amount of calories

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.960
to achieve a Shazam-worthy physique.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.600
When Variety quizzed him about his weight
gain at the Marvelous Mrs. Maisel season 2

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:22.310
premiere, the actor revealed that he'd been
taking on between 3000 and 4000 calories a

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.640
day ever since he won the lead role in the
DC movie.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.920
"Lemme just wolf down this peanut brittle
real quick…

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.040
Why would you do that?

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.240
Oh right, 'cause calories."

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.940
Levi went on to give a more detailed breakdown
of his Shazam! calorie count during his appearance

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.920
on Michael Rosenbaum's podcast:

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.760
"3,700 calories, then with a bunch of other
supplements like fish oil, Omega-3s."

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.340
It's an impressive amount of calories for
sure, but how does it match up against Levi's

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.430
DC counterparts?

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:56.870
The short answer is that, well, it doesn't:
both Ben Affleck and Henry Cavill reportedly

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:01.520
consumed up to 5,000 calories per day when
training to play Batman and Superman.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:07.600
Levi described his diet as "pretty lean and
clean," and he really wasn't kidding.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:11.769
To achieve his body goals the actor had to
give up some of his favorite snacks and make

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:16.300
every single mouthful count, which is why
most of his meals consist of protein-rich

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.280
chicken and large portions of broccoli, a
favorite of bodybuilders everywhere.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.280
Levi was even eating broccoli for breakfast
at one stage, documenting the experience on

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.400
Instagram stories.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.940
One bemused follower took to Twitter to ask
the actor why he would do such a thing, and

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.170
Levi revealed that he has a variation on chicken
and broccoli five times a day:

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:40.180
"I basically eat the same macros all day long:
meat and veg of varying combinations.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.560
I used to eat a lot of eggs in the morning,
but I think I have an intolerance to them."

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:48.380
Hopefully that means he didn't have to down
any raw egg shakes, Rocky style.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.180
Levi's physical transformation has clearly
been a source of inspiration to his fans,

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.280
with some even reaching out to ask the actor
for hints and tips on getting jacked.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.560
He told one of his followers:

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.320
"It's a marathon, not a sprint.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.299
I've been in the gym five days a week for
the last five months, and eaten pretty darn

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.600
healthy/strictly, but not so crazy that I'm
not still enjoying life.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.600
The system works."

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:15.680
When another fan asked how her skinny husband
could look more like Levi, the actor revealed

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.789
that he himself used to struggle with adding
muscle to his slender frame, and it was all

00:04:19.789 --> 00:04:20.680
down to diet.

00:04:20.909 --> 00:04:24.900
According to Levi, you can workout constantly,
but if you aren't providing your body with

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.919
all the right tools then you're going struggle
to improve on those newbie gains.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.409
The former Chuck star replied:

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.400
"The key, I found, was quite literally consuming
mass quantities.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.380
You have to feed your muscles.

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:39.789
You have to give your body the building material
necessary to grow larger.

00:04:39.789 --> 00:04:41.520
You have to eat, even when you're not hungry."

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:48.160
"14,000 calories later, I found myself down
at Subway, powering through a 12-inch veggie

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:48.760
on whole wheat."

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:54.780
Levi might advocate eating as much as humanly
possible, but that doesn't mean eating whatever

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:55.980
you can get your hands on.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:00.840
When he was asked how he manages to eat well
while still enjoying his life, he gave a pretty

00:05:00.969 --> 00:05:03.800
straightforward answer: avoid processed foods.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:08.279
"From my perspective, the biggest favor you
can do for yourself is avoiding all processed

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:08.780
foods.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.500
Sweet or savory, doesn't matter.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.500
It's all breaking down in your body as sugar,
that is then stored as fat.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.020
But there's a lot of tasty CLEAN food out
there.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.040
Get into it."

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.340
"Why are you eating stem first?"

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:21.820
"This is a new food for me.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:22.920
How else should I eat it?"

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.020
"The other way."

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:30.039
Junk food is far from the only obstacle when
you're trying to balance gym life with a social

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:30.540
life, however.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.419
Alcohol certainly doesn't help matters when
you're trying to remain as trim as possible.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.280
"I'd like to purchase some of your finest
beer, please."

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.219
Levi discovered the benefits of cutting out
the booze when he took part in Sober October

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:44.860
2018.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:45.960
The star admitted:

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.990
"It was a little difficult at first, and it's
still kinda strange not having a drink when

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:50.640
I do go out at night.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:54.780
But overall I feel so much healthier and happier
and clearer of mind and heart.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:55.800
It's been a good cleanse.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.040
May even take it longer.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:57.540
We'll see."

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:03.740
Finding the time to prepare five clean meals
a day can be a big challenge for anybody,

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:04.800
let alone a busy actor.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:08.660
But that's where having a major Hollywood
studio as your boss comes in handy.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.179
Levi praised Warner Bros. for helping him
reach his targets when he spoke to Michael

00:06:12.179 --> 00:06:17.270
Rosenbaum, revealing that the studio had arranged
for his meals to be brought right to his door.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:17.780
He said:

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.020
"I do meal delivery…

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:19.820
It's part of the job.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.960
And they've been very awesome about taking
care of me."

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.920
That's all well and good, but what does Levi
do when he's not home?

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:30.520
As an actor he has to travel a lot, but even
then he sticks to his regimented diet plan.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:31.340
He tweeted:

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:35.439
"I use different meal delivery companies in
different cities, because I need to eat a

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.560
lot through the day, and I don't know how
to cook.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:38.740
Like, at all."

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:43.580
Imagine putting yourself through months of
training and hundreds of portions of broccoli

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:46.920
only for one of the biggest names in fitness
to call you a fraud.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:52.360
That's the situation Levi found himself in
during March 2018, when Men's Health suggested

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.800
that the actor was wearing a padded suit on
set.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:59.800
Some behind the scenes photos of Levi in full
costume were leaked online, and regular contributor

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:04.349
Vinnie Mancuso took one look at the size of
Levi's biceps and called foul play.

00:07:04.349 --> 00:07:09.629
In response to the Men's Health investigation,
Levi posted a picture of his bicep on Twitter

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:12.260
along with the caption "Sooo much padding."

00:07:12.449 --> 00:07:16.640
It was the actor's way of getting back at
the fitness mag, but the author of the original

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.139
article wasn't convinced.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:23.840
In fact, Vinnie Mancuso said the photo Levi
posted was actually evidence that he was correct

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.640
about the suit padding all along.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.560
In a follow-up article, he said:

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.380
"Yes, that is a large arm.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:35.120
That is a gym-earned, above average sized
appendage [but] try to tell yourself honestly

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.320
that the arm in that photo is the same arm
[in the leaked photo].

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:39.040
You can't.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.340
You just can't do it."

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.920
Levi has had a hard time shaking the fake
muscle rumors since his spat with Men's Health.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:48.979
Some people seemed to think that he looked
padded out in a trailer that dropped in January

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.180
2019, with one fan questioning just how he
looked so huge.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:56.709
The actor gave a purposefully non-committal
answer, but that's likely because he's sick

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.280
of addressing the story by now.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.759
When Variety asked him about it on the red
carpet just a few weeks earlier, Levi again

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.659
denied that he needed extra mass.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.080
"Especially in this area.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.720
Does that look like fake?

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.040
Does that look fake to you?

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:10.580
Come on."

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:16.460
According to a study by the Society of Behavioral
Medicine, having a workout partner can greatly

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.360
improve your performance in the gym, doubling
cardio results in some instances.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.580
While many superhero actors are set up with
world-renowned trainers, the guy spotting

00:08:24.589 --> 00:08:27.219
Levi is actually a photographer by trade.

00:08:27.219 --> 00:08:32.029
Eric Blackmon has posted multiple pics and
videos of Levi pumping iron, unofficially

00:08:32.029 --> 00:08:33.940
documenting the actor's progress.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.560
In October 2017, Blackmon tweeted:

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:41.300
"Apparently I'll be getting ripped for Shazam!
as well, since Zachary Levi is kicking my

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.310
ass in the gym.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.200
I need protein.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:43.900
Now."

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.700
Despite the bleak winter weather, the pair
remained dedicated to the Shazam! cause as

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:50.060
2018 rolled around.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:55.040
By February, Levi was already looking far
more heroic in their sessions, and by May

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.080
both men were looking fighting fit.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:02.980
Levi replied to the second Men's Health article
with another photo of his guns, and this one

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.520
was harder to argue against.

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:09.470
The actor posted a topless pic of himself
in the gym, along with a hilarious equation.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.060
"It's like the old saying goes.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:16.640
Hard work, over time, plus chicken &amp; broccoli,
minus carbs, divided by whey protein, in which

00:09:16.649 --> 00:09:21.120
'X' represents the amount of supplements and
'Y' represents the sentiment of 'WHY the hell

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:26.440
am I doing this to myself?!', multiplied by
shameless selfies whilst staring into nowhere."

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.840
Talk about taking your workouts to the next
level.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.740
"Why is it so hard to understand?

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:36.840
This is not fffffff---ing string theory."

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.759
When he spoke to Variety in December 2018,
Levi was eager to discuss how being selected

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:46.220
to play the lead role in Shazam! changed his
life in more ways than one.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:50.560
His name is now known across the board in
Hollywood and he likely picked up a pretty

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.360
paycheck for his work on the Shazam!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:52.860
Movie.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.120
But he was also extremely grateful for the
chance to get healthy.

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:59.140
"Honestly, that's the stuff that I'm most
ecstatic about.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:03.240
Just the level of health that I've gotten
to, mental health, emotional health, spiritual

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:08.139
health, physical health, I am so jazzed about
that and I want to keep talking about that,

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.340
particularly mental health."

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:13.300
It would have been easy for Levi to give up
after Men's Health suggested that he just

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:17.560
wasn't big enough to play a superhero, but
he wasn't working out for anyone but himself.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:18.140
He added:

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:23.040
"I just feel like we're in a place, particularly
nowadays, where people need to be encouraged

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:28.040
and informed on what self-love is, and to
go and genuinely embrace themselves and love

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.600
themselves, so I'm really happy about all
of that."

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:35.120
"Sorry, I just had to reboot."

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:37.840
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:41.480
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
superheroes are coming soon.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:44.800
Subscribe to our YouTube channel, and hit
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

